35,2,1,talk,Minato,,The treasurer spends six hours a month chasing session money. Mid-year joiners also need a lot of manual calculations.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Seventy percent of our costs are fixed, like insurance. Also, a third of renewals are late or need monthly installments.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"Past named grades caused friction and discouraged lower tiers. Also, many non-joiners refuse to commit to a full year upfront.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,Turnout dropped after the summer door charges. Some quiet members also feel uneasy about the cost per visit.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's a mess. A quarter of us do two-thirds of the attending, and the same nine people do all the setup.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, if most costs are fixed, does that mean we must have a base fee?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,Precisely. We cannot guess our way through fixed overheads without risking the account.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,But @May's point about the summer outings suggests that charging per event pushes people away.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly. People stop feeling like the club is ""theirs"" when they have to pay every time they walk in.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"While that's true, it's unfair that the regulars carry the weight while others pay the same for nothing.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,I just don't want the next treasurer to quit. Chasing small amounts every week sounds exhausting.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,A single annual collection is much more efficient for the books and the budget.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,But we can't ignore the people who won't commit to a full year. We'll lose new members.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,We need something that feels welcoming but doesn't make people hesitate at the door.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Efficiency is fine, but we need to address the imbalance of use and effort.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
